Wait, the hashchange will call `render()` which will read from localStorage. But the filter was already set to the same value, so the data should be there. Let me test.

Actually there's another subtlety. The `loadApp` creates a new Window, but the `navigate` helper and `hashchange` wiring from world.js might not be set up yet for the new window. Let me check world.js more carefully.

Looking at world.js:
```js
loadApp() {
    // ...
    this.document.write(fs.readFileSync(indexPath, 'utf8'));
    this.document.close();
    this.window.eval(appSource);
    this.document.dispatchEvent(new this.window.Event('DOMContentLoaded', { bubbles: true }));
    this.window.dispatchEvent(new this.window.Event('load'));

    // ROUTING. ...
    const w = this.window;
    this.document.addEventListener('click', (e) => { ... }, true);
    return this.document;
}
```

So the routing click handler is set up on the new document. And hashchange handler is set up in the app. So dispatching hashchange should work.

Let me test.

